    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Objectives (30-day rolling window)\n\n| SLO | Objective | Budget | Fast burn (page) | Slow burn (ticket) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Availability | 99.9% of requests without a 5xx | 0.1% | 14.4x over 1h **and** 5m | 6x over 6h **and** 30m |\n| Latency | 99% of requests under 300 ms | 1% | 14.4x over 1h **and** 5m | 6x over 6h **and** 30m |\n\nA burn rate of 1 spends the budget in exactly 30 days. 14.4 spends it in two, 6 spends it in five. The short window in each pair exists so the alert resolves when the incident does; it is a guard, not a second opinion. The arithmetic is in `slo/README.md`."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Availability",
      "collapsed": false,
